[38;5;231m⏺[39m Using hyperpowers:brainstorming. This looks [1mbounded[0m — [38;5;153mindex.html[39m is a single static page with an empty [38;5;153m<main>[39m, and a
  checkbox drops straight into it. So I'll ask one question, present a short design in chat, and skip the spec/plan
  documents.

  One thing genuinely forks here. The page has no items yet — [38;5;153m<main>[39m is empty — so "mark items as done" can mean two
  different deliverables:

  - [1mOne checkbox + label, hardcoded in the HTML.[0m Cheapest, zero JS, matches "nothing fancy" literally. Costs you nothing
    to change later, but it doesn't give you anything to reuse when real items arrive.
  - [1mA small JS function that renders a checkbox row per item[0m, called with a hardcoded array for now. Slightly more code,
    and it commits you to a (trivial) item shape, but it's the piece you'd actually keep once tasks come from somewhere
    real.

  Neither is expensive to undo at this size. I lean toward the reusable function — "items" (plural) in your request
  suggests a list is coming, and the difference is about ten lines.
